title: 'Warpline flight-readiness: seven things we believed, measured against what is actually true'
summary: 'Pre-flight for the first real Warpline field test (an Expo/React Native app). Every load-bearing belief carried into this session was checked against the code or a falsifier rather than inherited. Seven were wrong — four in Warpline''s favour, three against it — and two of the wrong ones were mine, produced during this session. The dress rehearsal passed end to end (first genuine KNOT), the 40-seal scale run passed all six pre-registered criteria, and four defects were fixed: lens ignore-blindness, health blindness to native KNOTs, cold-agent unreachability of the write path, and a git worktree TOCTOU race. A fifth — renames grading as destruction — was found by the scale run itself.'
