body: |-
  THE SHAPE OF THIS ENTRY: each item is BELIEVED -> ACTUAL -> CONSEQUENCE. The point is not the individual corrections but the base rate, which is the calibration datum worth keeping.

  1. BELIEVED: the ledger was polluted with build output; a correction seal would retire ~16,015 symbols. ACTUAL: the sealed ledger was NEVER polluted. Seals absorb a git ref, which materialises through `git archive` = git-tracked files only, and every junk source (.build/, **/target/, .mcp.json) is gitignored. Live counts across the fix: 9325 -> 9327, a delta of +2, which was this session's own new file. The 55.9%-junk figure was real but belonged to `absorb WORKTREE` — the surface behind `status`, `diff` and worktree-mode absorbs. CONSEQUENCE: a false alarm delivered to the founder, caught only because he asked "holy, we are retiring that many symbols?". Warpline has THREE absorb surfaces with different visibility; a measurement that does not name its surface will be read as global.

  2. BELIEVED (checkpoint): 13,179 of 16,035 born symbols came from `.build/** or node_modules`. ACTUAL: 14,168 of 25,341, node_modules contributes exactly ZERO, and the mechanism is cfg-lens lifting every JSON key as a symbol (one Swift output-file-map.json yields 927), not the snapshot path. Those ids also embedded absolute machine paths, making the state's content-address machine-dependent. CONSEQUENCE: acting on the inherited number would have produced a fix aimed at the wrong walker entirely.

  3. BELIEVED: ZERO KNOTs had ever been produced; the denominator was structurally empty. ACTUAL: partly an instrument artifact. `warpline health` counted contested verdicts only from shadow rows, while the NATIVE path — the one agents use — persists payloads to .warpline/knots/ and writes no shadow row. A real KNOT sat on disk while the diagnostic printed "ZERO contested verdicts". The lifecycle itself worked on the first honest attempt: genesis -> fork x2 -> propose x2 -> FAST_ADMIT -> KNOT with hydrated payload -> human resolve.

  4. BELIEVED: the write path was usable by a cold agent (F4 / TD-2026-07-21-766). ACTUAL: I could not complete the cycle from --help with the source open. `admit --native` returned NOOP three times. The CLI marked --claim REQUIRED while the engine requires `intent` and treats claim as optional, forcing an agent to author `#code:<file>::<name>` symbol-id syntax the CLI never teaches; and admit-after-fork-without-propose reported "the agent changed no meaning", which is false when the work is real and merely unsealed.

  5. BELIEVED: one known flaky test (essence-iterative, 25k-deep, load-sensitive). ACTUAL: a genuine concurrency bug. Every `git worktree add` named its leaf `tree`, and git registers worktrees under `.git/worktrees/<basename>`, de-duplicating by check-then-create — a TOCTOU window. Concurrent adds against one repo raced, surfacing as three DIFFERENT unrelated tests failing across three runs. Suite went from 997/109 with 1-3 load-dependent failures to 1006/110 stable across consecutive runs.

  6. BELIEVED (product claim, in CLI help and the sem-delta header): renames are the EMPTY delta. ACTUAL: true for .purpose symbols, structurally impossible for code-units — a code-unit's symbol embeds the file path, so the contentId-equal rename branch was unreachable. Measured on the 40-seal run: 12 of 42 strands graded `overturned` with confidence 0.8 -> 0.35, every one a file move whose body never changed, because `grade` overturns a strand whose symbols a later strand RETIRES. Routine refactoring was degrading the per-codebase calibration signal — the moat. After the fix: 0 overturned, 29 survived, 0 retirements, 10 renamed-noop.

  7. BELIEVED (open task T-2026-06-13-004): the learning loop only PRINTS advice. ACTUAL: out of date — the chain is wired at task-loader.ts:556, but gated on `isTerminalStatus && parentTaskId` plus whole-sibling-set settlement, and only 53 of 231 tasks carry a parent. The deeper finding is separate and worse: `orchestrate_inline` silently drops 18 of 26 rostered agents (manifest holds 8), so Loid — who owns the learning loop — cannot be dispatched at all. Filed as T-2026-08-11-007; deferred by founder decision until Warpline's flight version is settled.

  WHERE THINGS ACTUALLY STAND. Lifecycle verified end to end on a fresh repo. Expo-shaped absorb yields 13 real symbols where it would have yielded 3,673 (99.6% junk). Scale run: 40 seals, all six pre-registered criteria pass, marginal cost per seal DECREASING with depth (0.53x), latency flat (0.98x), 0.84 MB total, byte-identical restore at depth 41. Cold-agent path reachable from --help alone. 21 commits unpushed; push has never been authorised.

  STILL OPEN, all previously flagged as founder decisions rather than blockers: oracle.ts:160 shares the merge-tree bad-ref conflation (git merge-tree exits 1 for BOTH "conflicted" and "not a ref"); states/ has no replication path and a lost state file is a permanent fail-closed; the soundness-audit doc is stale; the standing-report artifact needs Rev 3.
